WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:04.850
While it might look like it's nothing but
glitz and glamor, a ton of unseen work goes

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.080
into making television.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.490
For actors, it can lead to even more labor
especially if they share a hand in writing,

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:11.700
producing, or directing.

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:16.800
While acting can be a difficult and demanding
job, actors are paid massive amounts of money

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:17.860
to make up for it.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:21.930
Still, even among the wealthiest actors in
Hollywood, these television celebrities take

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:22.420
the cake.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.700
Here are tv stars who took home shockingly
huge paychecks.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.560
Like all sitcoms, The Big Bang Theory depends
on a consistent, likable cast.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:35.100
It was almost no surprise when the central
trio Kaley Cuoco, Johnny Galecki, and Jim

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:40.740
Parsons were able to negotiate a salary bump
to $1,000,000 each per episode before season

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.240
10.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:45.940
The surprise is that they actually gave some
of it back, as they later took a $100,000

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.100
pay cut to help their fellow cast members
earn their own sizable bump.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:49.640
Nice!

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:54.379
When it comes to well-paid sitcom actors,
you can't ignore the cast of Friends, who

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:58.580
managed to capture audiences' hearts and NBC
Universal's wallet all at once.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:02.829
While the cast might have gone their separate
ways after the show ended, they banded together

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:05.100
for equal paychecks in the final seasons.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.560
"What's more important, your friends or your
money?"

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.080
"Friends!

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:14.300
"Friends."

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.579
It turns out you can have both.

00:01:16.579 --> 00:01:20.549
The popularity of the show meant the cast
had a massive amount of bargaining power and

00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:25.719
the six stars took advantage by entering into
a joint negotiation for a cool $1 mil each

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:27.800
per episode for seasons nine and ten.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:33.119
For the Netflix-produced continuation of Gilmore
Girls, Alexis Bledel and Lauren Graham both

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:37.310
managed to score an impressive $750,000 per
episode.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:39.780
That's enough money to buy delivery food for
the rest of their lives.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.320
"The whole point of getting everything within
delivery distance is so we can judge the quality

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:47.140
of food, speed of service, and cuteness of
delivery guys on a scale from 1 to 10.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.260
We cannot work from memory on this."

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:52.440
As Game of Thrones has killed off most of
its cast, it's become a lot clearer which

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:56.679
characters are the real protagonists in the
show; as you might expect, this revelation

00:01:56.679 --> 00:02:01.619
led to some powerful bargaining chips for
these actors: Variety reported in 2016 that

00:02:01.619 --> 00:02:06.330
Kit Harington, Lena Headey, Peter Dinklage,
Emilia Clarke, and Nikolaj Coster-Waldau all

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:09.460
managed to grab a cool $500,000 per episode.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:16.760
"And of course, you have heard the phrase,
'a Lannister always pays his debts."

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.880
And it seems like HBO does too.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.900
Doctors tend to be well-paid, but playing
a doctor on television is even more lucrative.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:30.850
Ellen Pompeo of Grey's Anatomy receives $575,000
per episode of the long-running medical drama.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:35.400
The show is still incredibly successful after
over a dozen seasons, but what did Pompeo

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.400
do to deserve such a high paycheck?

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.099
Pompeo told The Hollywood Reporter:

00:02:39.099 --> 00:02:42.120
"The truth is, anybody can be good on a show
season one and two.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:44.489
Can you be good 14 years later?

00:02:44.489 --> 00:02:45.840
Now, that's a f-----' skill."

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:50.360
He might be more well-known as a film star,
but Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson has been making

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:53.260
a pretty tidy sum of money as a television
star too.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:58.200
Johnson stars in the HBO show Ballers, which
follows a financial manager negotiating deals

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.440
for his slightly-less massive clients.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:05.879
For his part in the show, Johnson earned a
cool $650,000 per episode enough to vault

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:10.240
him onto this list, even without including
his movie star paychecks in between episodes.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:14.380
The Big Little Lies stars are drawing some
very big paychecks.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:18.640
In advance of the award-winning HBO hit's
second season, leads Reese Witherspoon and

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:22.540
Nicole Kidman negotiated to earn over $1,000,000
per episode.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:26.120
That's the benefit of being A-list movie stars
appearing in a prestige drama.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:31.439
Combining a genial personality and a deep
roster of celebrity friends, Ellen DeGeneres

00:03:31.439 --> 00:03:34.180
has built a full-blown multimedia empire.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:40.220
In 2017, her estimated annual income reached
$50 million, and that was calculated before

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.340
the premiere of her new show Game of Games.

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:46.600
At this rate, DeGeneres could probably give
out her own money on her game show and still

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:47.460
come out ahead.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:52.020
What's left to say about Oprah that her massive
media empire hasn't said already?

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:56.239
Her syndicated television show made her millions,
along with all the numerous sponsorships and

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:59.010
merchandising deals that came from listing
her "favorite things."

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:04.680
In fact, she's so successful at media entrepreneurship,
it's difficult to find out what she made strictly

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.100
from her television series.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:11.110
We do know that in 2011, which included the
final season of The Oprah Winfrey Show, she

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:16.670
took home an estimated $290 million - and
that was reportedly a major pay cut from the

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:17.480
previous year.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:22.460
Her total wealth is worth more than the GDP
of some countries, and she's the only billionaire

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.320
on this list.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:24.800
"You get a car!

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:25.780
You get a car!

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:29.780
EVERYBODY GETS A CAR!"

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:35.760
According to the Washington Post, Judge Judy
star Judith Sheindlin makes a mind-boggling

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:41.780
$47 million for only 52 days of work, meaning
that she makes almost $1 million a day.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:43.600
Wondering about the secret to her success?

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:48.660
It's apparently an absolutely ruthless negotiating
tactic of refusing to negotiate.

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:50.180
Judy told the Hollywood Reporter:

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:54.040
"We sit across the table, and I hand him the
envelope and I say, 'Don't read it now, let's

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.040
have a nice dinner.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.040
Call me tomorrow.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:56.800
You want it, fine.

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:58.780
Otherwise, I'll produce it myself.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:00.040
That's the negotiation."

